FolkTech internal QA audit generated from Augment + Jarvis review.
Issues are tracked in `.ftai` format for clarity, export, and validation.

---
@issue
id: 001
severity: critical
location: PocketMedic/Features/Calculators/DrugDosageCalculatorView.swift
description: Medication file fails silently if not found. Returns empty array with no error surfaced to user. try? swallows error. No retry or alert.
recommendation: Implement `MedicationLoadError` enum. Add user-visible alert and retry option. Avoid silent fail fallback.
status: open
@end

@issue
id: 002
severity: critical
location: extra files/Paramedic Pocket/MainView.swift
description: Query processing lacks input sanitization, error handling, offline check, or retry. Clears input before processing completes.
recommendation: Use async error-handled flow. Add timeout logic. Store pre-cleared input for retry. Implement `QueryError` enum.
status: open
@end

@issue
id: 003
severity: critical
location: extra files/Paramedic Pocket/LocalLLMManager.swift
description: handleMemoryWarning() creates new instance instead of cleaning up. No user notification. No thread-safety or recovery strategy.
recommendation: Use `DispatchQueue` + `NSLock`. Notify user via NotificationCenter. Proper unload + recovery plan with logs.
status: open
@end

@issue
id: 004
severity: critical
location: extra files/Paramedic Pocket/Models/MedicalProtocol.swift
description: Silent fallback to default protocols. No integrity check, versioning, or error notification. Blocking main thread with file I/O.
recommendation: Async load with error throws. Add version check, content validation, and user alert. Avoid main-thread data loading.
status: open
@end

@issue
id: 005
severity: moderate
location: extra files/Paramedic Pocket/Models/Managers.swift.bak
description: RAGManager is a placeholder. No actual RAG logic. No validation, error handling, or production use safeguards.
recommendation: Replace with actual TinyBERT RAG or SQL-based fallback. Add input validation, async handling, and monitoring.
status: open
@end
